ady in-progress tasks for tr that have completed earlier requirement sets. The requirement_states list only shows what's currently available for new work, not what's already been finished, so the completed requirements for tr aren't showing up as \"ready\" anymore.\n\nLet me check the actual status field in requirement_states — they're all marked as \"ready\", which means they're all available for task proposals. But I need to reconcile this with the code_status and package_contracts to understand what's actually been implemented versus what still needs work. Looking at what's actually in requirement_states, I see requirements scattered across multiple releases—srd004-ts in 15.0, then srd053 through srd078 spanning releases 07.0 through 08.1. The earlier packages like srd001, srd002, and srd003 aren't tracked here, which suggests their requirements are either all resolved or not yet ready for the current release cycle. I'm noticing that srd111-ptx is in release 15.0, then there's a jump back to srd112-chronic through srd114-vidir in release 14.0. Looking at the earlier releases, most of the code from 00.0 through 06.1 is already implemented, but there are several use cases marked as \"not started\" without corresponding requirements in the system—like format, testutils, cat, nproc, and ls. Looking at the requirement states, release 07.0 is the earliest with ready requirements. I'm checking what's available across the tools in that release—srd053-sort has 3 ready requirements, while srd054-tr has 6 ready requirements available.\n\nNow I need to verify the weights for each requirement against the 4-point limit per task, but the requirements.yaml file isn't provided in the context, so I can't determine the exact weights needed to propose valid task combinations. I need to work with default weight assumptions since I can't access the requirements file, so I'll stick with the max 4 requirements per task constraint as my safety limit. Now I'm mapping out the task breakdow